    "details": "https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/SkX7Pmiofg reports:\n\n> Vifm 0.8.1-beta through 0.14.4 reuses a pre-existing IPC FIFO in the\n> shared temporary directory without checking ownership, allowing local\n> users to execute commands as another user. Attackers can pre-create a\n> world-writable vifm-ipc-vifm FIFO and write IPC packets with -c and !\n> shell commands that execute with the victim\\'s privileges.\n",
